title The slice that says where it cut
prompt Keaton -- take the bounded slice door
think The fields sit BESIDE the whole captures rather than replacing them, so a script that wants every byte still has it and only the SAYING is bounded. Replacing them would have fixed the message by breaking every reader.
think 512 bytes is derived rather than chosen: the composed message must fit 4,096 with its prose around it and room for a second capture in the same sentence, and eight briefs still fit.
obs HEAD FOR ERR AND TAIL FOR OUT, and the asymmetry is the whole design. A compiler names its error first and elaborates after; a program's last words are its reason. Both are real cases from the two captures that opened this row rather than a guess about which end matters.
obs THE CUT IS SAID. A brief that was cut carries N more bytes or N earlier bytes, so a reader can tell a short reason from a truncated one -- which is the exact distinction the silent fallback destroyed.
obs THE CLIFF IS A LEG OF THE CONTROL rather than only a memory. A tree that forgot why these fields exist would drift back to composing whole captures, so the control asserts that a whole capture STILL goes literal past 4,096 beside asserting that a brief does not.
obs EVERY LEG RUNS FROM BOTH SIDES. A brief proven only on long input cannot be told from a field that always truncates, so each is checked short and unmarked as hard as it is checked long and marked.
obs I BUILT THE INTERPRETER TO A PEN BEFORE TOUCHING THE LIVE ONE, ran seven standing witnesses green under it, kept the elder binary aside, and only then installed. Rishi runs every guard in this tree, so a bad build there is not a red, it is a stop.
obs WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH, named rather than quietly left: say_compose_bound still reads 551 per mille against 489, exactly as before this lap. The briefs give that ratchet a way DOWN, since a site composing a brief is bounded by construction, yet I swept no site -- that breach predates the lap and wants its own word.
loom brief max_brief_bytes=512 cliff=4096 fields_added=2 control_legs=13 faults=0
loom install pen_built=yes witnesses_under_new=7 red=0 rostered_total=376
loom ratchet say_compose_deferred_per_mille=551 ceiling=489 unchanged=yes
rota none -- a door taken on Keaton's word, no rota this lap
